# Source and docs: normalise to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Evidence and commitments: NEVER touched by git.
#
# This is not a style preference. A captured packet is committed by its BLAKE3
# hash, and `cosign` signs manifest bytes. If git rewrote a CRLF on checkout —
# or normalised one on commit — the bytes on disk would no longer be the bytes
# that were hashed and signed, and every proof over that record would fail
# verification for a reason no one would think to look for.
archive/**  -text
artifacts/** -text
state/**    -text
